.task-board/EPIC-260715-2mqgvm_viability-and-foundation/STORY-260715-2itwz7_apple-platform-intent-gate/README.md:10:1. A dated evidence dossier cites the controlling Apple sources and describes the complete packet, TCP, SSH, DNS, and exit-host behavior without euphemism. 2. The dossier identifies the TN3120 ambiguity and asks a decision-capable Apple channel a concrete intended-use and distribution question. 3. Gate evidence is one of the accepted forms: written DTS response, entitlement or review feedback for an accurately disclosed prototype, or an approved architecture change that carries packet semantics to a remote VPN endpoint. 4. Reproducible artifacts record submission text, dates, case or review identifiers, responses, redactions, and source revision. 5. A decision record declares pass, fail, or pivot, states constraints and affected downstream work, and leaves production tasks blocked on any negative or ambiguous result.
