.task-board/EPIC-260715-21g2pi_product-experience-and-security/STORY-260715-309t4z_connection-control-and-status-ui/README.md:10:1. iOS and macOS users can select an eligible profile, grant required system VPN permission, connect, disconnect, and recover after containing-app relaunch while the Network Extension session remains authoritative. 2. The UI renders exactly the required lifecycle states and never reports connected/full unless the current provider generation confirms TCP, leak-safe DNS, UDP, and required address-family capability. 3. Degraded mode remains connected, names the missing UDP capability and safe limitations, while failed is reserved for a mandatory safe-forwarding failure. 4. Reasserting, disconnecting, stale snapshots, permission denial, configuration failure, host trust/auth failure, and tunnel setup failure have deterministic controls and accessible remediation. 5. QUIC and routing settings expose only policies supported by the accepted M3 contracts, explain compatible versus fail-closed limitations, and apply through versioned profile generations. 6. Deterministic state tests, iOS/macOS UI tests, and physical-device checks verify controls, system VPN indicator, host-app termination continuity, full/degraded transitions, profile switching, accessibility, and screenshots.
