.task-board/EPIC-260715-21g2pi_product-experience-and-security/STORY-260715-3tds7d_diagnostics-privacy-and-support/README.md:10:1. Default diagnostics are bounded and limited to approved timestamps, states, lane identifiers, aggregate counts, error domains/codes, memory observations, negotiated algorithms, relay identity, and redacted address-family facts. 2. Automated adversarial tests prove keys, passphrases, packet payloads, DNS names, destination hosts or IPs, full local addresses, shell input, and traffic samples cannot enter logs, snapshots, crash annotations, or support exports. 3. A user can inspect diagnostic categories, preview the exact export manifest, create an export only on explicit action, and delete retained local support data on iOS and macOS. 4. Before first VPN enablement the app explains processed data, the user-controlled SSH exit, exit-host visibility, Relux Works absence from the baseline data path, system-excluded traffic, retention/deletion, and zero traffic telemetry. 5. Extension-to-app diagnostic transfer is versioned, size-bounded, stale-generation safe, and remains useful after containing-app relaunch. 6. Unit, property/fuzz where appropriate, UI, and physical acceptance tests verify redaction, bounds, disclosure gating, export preview/output, deletion, accessibility, and no analytics or traffic-telemetry endpoints.
