.resources/TASK-260715-1tnjlu/TASK-260715-1tnjlu_review-focus.md:1:Independent architecture review focus. Verify the proposed ADR and task-scoped decision against every AC, accepted specs, and cited primary RFC evidence; do not accept merely because the policy is vendor-neutral. Challenge whether explicit ordered numeric IPv4/IPv6 dns53 profile endpoints plus SSH DNS-over-TCP are implementable from the exit and genuinely eliminate ordinary-query use of the physical resolver after routes. Trace the only allowed pre-route physical DNS use for SSH-host bootstrap and ensure the actual SSH endpoint is captured so reconnect and ordinary DNS do not create circularity or silent fallback. Audit exact profile field names, cardinalities, canonical address validation, IPv4/IPv6 order, port defaults, transport, client UDP/TCP handling, truncation, DNSSEC transparency, cache generation, retry versus resolver shopping, timeout/failure/teardown, migration, disabled-profile state, privacy, M2 relay/degraded semantics, and M4 impacts. Confirm any timeout/in-flight numbers are explicitly injectable evidence baselines with justified hard caps, not claimed final physical tuning. Confirm DoH, exit-host discovery, product default, shell parsing, fake DNS, and unapproved public resolver choices are rejected for evidence-backed reasons. Inspect new TASK-260721-33o8fc and TASK-260721-2raag7 descriptions, AC, resources, and dependency links for completeness and absence of duplicate or over-broad work. Render or inspect the diagram for correctness and legibility; run board/spec/link/hash/XML/diff consistency checks. Treat reviewer acceptance as accountable architecture approval only if the choice follows entirely from the already accepted goal and security invariants; otherwise route to blocked with the exact human product decision. Attach a task-scoped verdict and route accepted work to done or changes to analysis.
